{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"body":"Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.\n\nInspected: Configured challenge assertions, their relevant definitions and the cited audited paper statements were compared.\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:a9bf40a317be18a3bb4b02b0b5b512d58f6098539c78bfd0cff8a41dbe4783c5","fingerprint":"sha256:8a36a08b7717ec03b64f44559d4196feae88ac3e7724ba669c6ff219885b751d","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:ef587bd9705fab80eefa31aa07255c6db5b443720a7a8b4ea238a8ed8a30a6e4","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Thorp.Current.first_reciprocal_main"],"explanation":"The first formal conjunct bounds the sum of reciprocal Specht degrees uniformly in positive n and sends the sum over positive-defect shapes to zero. These are the u=1 cases of the paper inverse-degree-sum theorem and its Z_u convergence. The formal theorem also contains a separate Fourier bound, covered by the orbit-lift link.","fingerprint":"sha256:e97e1f75d29e87dfa80aac4ca4c45ea9123c208326fc8f0983f7492461247284","limitations":"The identification of positive defect with omission of the trivial and sign shapes is read from the partition/longest-row-or-column definitions; it is not independently proof-checked.","relation":"formal-is-consequence","row_id":"From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026#l:degree-all-powers","statement_sha256":"sha256:b29f166e84994f2eccdbfd57e29335c677d24238cd5f1c6157a042bce7e64229"},{"declarations":["OAI.Thorp.Current.first_reciprocal_main"],"explanation":"The second formal conjunct uses eight equal blocks on 2^d positions, d>=3, cap four and an irreducible unitary representation, giving operator norm at most sqrt(32*C1)*D^(-5/16). These constants and assumptions match the orbit-lift proposition. The proposition permits every positive multiple of eight, whereas the formal assertion restricts cardinality to powers of two.","fingerprint":"sha256:54c8aaf13da946b56e397373905d3f09a1f869bf08406fb379926209eb9097d0","limitations":"This link covers the Fourier-bound conjunct only; the reciprocal-degree-sum conjunct has a separate source link.","relation":"formal-is-part","row_id":"Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026#prop:orbit-lift","statement_sha256":"sha256:b5d63b0cdaa7756bd5c001f963e6849a13df4dac1304b308cd252915ed5f7619"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/ThorpFirstReciprocal.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/degrees.tex#L162","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Optimal-order-mixing-of-the-Thorp-shuffle-September-26-2026/build/main.tex#L486"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:ThorpFirstReciprocal","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/4fa7b8d32c857852fc1ba17f.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/4fa7b8d32c857852fc1ba17f.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/4fa7b8d32c857852fc1ba17f.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/4fa7b8d32c857852fc1ba17f.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/4fa7b8d32c857852fc1ba17f.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.Thorp.Current.first_reciprocal_main","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/ThorpFirstReciprocal.lean","line":205,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"ef587bd9705fab80eefa31aa07255c6db5b443720a7a8b4ea238a8ed8a30a6e4","statement_sha256":"sha256:dd45af9070fa09abb533bfa5629544295a64068264cb730a7f7274d85575f64a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/ThorpFirstReciprocal.lean#L205"},"text":"theorem first_reciprocal_main :\n    (BddAbove (Set.range (fun n : {n : ℕ // 1 ≤ n} => reciprocalFirst n.val)) ∧\n    (∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → reciprocalFirst n ≤ C1) ∧\n    Tendsto exceptionalFirst atTop (nhds 0)) ∧\n    (∀ (d : ℕ) (_hd : 3 ≤ d)\n    (e : Position d ≃ Fin 8 × Fin (2 ^ (d - 3)))\n    {E : Type uE} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℂ E]\n    (ρ : Representation ℂ (Equiv.Perm (Position d)) E)\n    [Representation.IsIrreducible ρ]\n    (_ : ∀ g x y, ⟪ρ g x, ρ g y⟫_ℂ = ⟪x, y⟫_ℂ)\n    (ν : Equiv.Perm (Position d) → ℝ)\n    (_ : ∀ g, 0 ≤ ν g) (_ : ∑ g, ν g = 1)\n    (_ : ∀ (i : Fin 8) (g : Equiv.Perm (Position d)),\n      ∑ h : Equiv.Perm (Fin (2 ^ (d - 3))),\n          ν (g * Block.embedding e (Pi.mulSingle i h)) ≤\n        4 * (Fintype.card (Equiv.Perm (Fin (2 ^ (d - 3)))) : ℝ) /\n          Fintype.card (Equiv.Perm (Position d))),\n    ‖LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap (Fourier.integrated ρ (fun g => (ν g : ℂ)))‖ ≤\n      Real.sqrt (32 * C1) * (Module.finrank ℂ E : ℝ) ^ (-5 / 16 : ℝ))"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"l:ThorpFirstReciprocal","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[],"pairings":{"f:238":{"alternatives":["pair:ce58d8fa75d4e50a4d46664f","pair:253dc210b46a2bf4c4bd9ce6","pair:e4f066016bd25b57199d35a3","pair:6de1b8e829f9c6adb1433e6c","pair:e69934e530951ec7e7499ad0","pair:1dab794e5d360bf521c6ae33","pair:598ed2671993647652947df1","pair:5392b10810e3fb311e187e00","pair:92a7c65c14418714a2f16dbf","pair:bd5e57d9bdd5c3e5df4d5a82","pair:a7fd16a1c928d587f83361db","pair:d01fee47c5edeb2e4b70fa2a","pair:57b48be772dcd0129b1c72f6","pair:1d156a2bc32a81f7d53f1f34","pair:9a29d9822abd0aed7432b88a","pair:5495563c1c3e906be2be5834"],"contributed_readings":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"content_sha256":"sha256:a9bf40a317be18a3bb4b02b0b5b512d58f6098539c78bfd0cff8a41dbe4783c5","decision":"linked","detail":{"path":"lean-previews/4fa7b8d32c857852fc1ba17f.json","pointer":"/contributions/0"},"provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"review_state":"unreviewed","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Thorp.Current.first_reciprocal_main"],"general_disclaimer":false,"limitations":"The identification of positive defect with omission of the trivial and sign shapes is read from the partition/longest-row-or-column definitions; it is not independently proof-checked.","relation":"formal-is-consequence","target":"r:From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026:l:degree-all-powers"},{"declarations":["OAI.Thorp.Current.first_reciprocal_main"],"general_disclaimer":false,"limitations":"This link covers the Fourier-bound conjunct only; the reciprocal-degree-sum conjunct has a separate source link.","relation":"formal-is-part","target":"r:Optimal-order-m